    "intro_narrative": "You stand in the cold, blue glow of the defunct Arasaka Sub-Net server room. Rain drums rhythmically against the reinforced glass high above the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Veridia. You are a 'Diver,' a data archeologist hired to retrieve a legendary piece of pre-War tech: the data contents of a specific Neuro-Cortex Chip. The chip isn't just lying around; it has to be synthesized and programmed on-site using the facility's dormant industrial equipment. The room is filled with whirring processors, locked terminals, and cryptographic nodes. You must restore the data flow, bypass the security protocols, and fabricate the vessel to smuggle the data out before the intrusion countermeasures incinerate the room—and you along with it.",
    "narrative_style": "cyberpunk"
  },
